<section>
  <h2>Summary</h2>
  <p class="lede">For 57 minutes on Monday 28 September, about a third of customer payment confirmations failed with HTTP 503. 1,444 of 4,694 confirmation requests failed; cart and browsing were not affected.</p>
  <p>At 09:36 the payments team released payments-gw v5.2, which added a synchronous fraud check to the confirm path. The check was behind the flag <code>fraud_check_sync</code>, but the flag defaulted to ON, so it went live for all traffic at deploy. Two other conditions made this an outage. fraud-svc was running on 2 replicas after a cost change the previous Friday. Then at 09:40 the "Autumn sale" email went to 1.2M customers and roughly doubled confirmation traffic. fraud-svc saturated, fraud calls hit the 3 s timeout, and payments-gw returned 503 for the confirmation.</p>
  <p>Scaling fraud-svc to 6 replicas at 10:25 cut the failure rate roughly in half. Turning the flag off at 10:40 ended the errors immediately. Responders initially investigated a CDN change and a planned database failover; the v5.2 release was identified 45 minutes after the alert.</p>
  <p>The RCA rates this cause <strong>strongly supported</strong>, not confirmed: the v5.2 path has not yet been re-tested under load. We do not yet know how many of the failed confirmations turned into lost orders.</p>
</section>

