  <h3>Customers</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>1,444 of 4,694 confirmation requests failed (30.8%)</strong> between 09:42:52 and 10:40:00, from edge logs on both edges (edge-02 clock corrected by −95 s).</li>
    <li>1,420 were 503s from the fraud-check path. 24 were 502s during the ~20 s orders-db failover at 10:05, which affected all paths.</li>
    <li>The failure rate was about 35% before mitigation, 10–20% after fraud-svc was scaled to 6 replicas at 10:25, and zero from 10:40.</li>
    <li>Cart, browsing and checkout pages loaded normally. Only the final payment confirmation failed.</li>
    <li><strong>Not measured:</strong> how many customers retried successfully, how many abandoned the order, and the revenue effect. This is the main gap in this report (action 10).</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>SLO and error budget</h3>
  <p>SLO: 99.5% of payment confirmation requests succeed, measured at the edge per calendar month. Every failed edge request counts, including the 24 DB-failover 502s.</p>
