## Code Review: feature/batch-send (8ad6659)

### Summary
**Request Changes.** Both files have blocking bugs. `sendOne` now retries forever, and `sendCampaign` returns before any message is sent, so it reports success even when every send fails.

### Critical Issues
| # | File | Line | Issue | Severity |
|---|------|------|-------|----------|
| 1 | src/send.ts | 7 | **Infinite retry loop.** The `attempt++` was removed from the `for` header and the `attempt === MAX_ATTEMPTS` check was dropped, so `attempt` stays at 1. Any 5xx, 429 or network error now retries every 400ms with no end. During an outage every recipient's send hangs and keeps hitting the API. | 🔴 Critical |
| 2 | src/batch.ts | 10–12 | **Fire-and-forget sends.** `forEach` ignores the promises its async callback returns, so `sendCampaign` returns `{ sent: recipients.length }` before any send finishes. `sent` is the recipient count, not the number delivered. Rejections from `sendOne` become unhandled promise rejections (Bun/Node may crash or log and drop them), and the caller can't detect failures. | 🔴 Critical |
| 3 | src/batch.ts | 10 | **No concurrency limit.** A large campaign starts N requests at once. That causes the 429s this PR is trying to handle, and together with #1 every throttled request then retries forever. | 🔴 High |
| 4 | src/batch.ts | 7–9 | **Connection leak.** The `try/finally` was removed, so if `conn.query` throws, `conn.release()` never runs. Repeated failures will exhaust the pool. | 🟠 High |

### Suggestions
| # | File | Line | Suggestion | Category |
|---|------|------|------------|----------|
| 1 | src/send.ts | 4 | For 429, use the server's `Retry-After` value when it's present instead of a fixed backoff. `HttpError` currently only carries `status`, so this means extending it. Add jitter as well, so parallel sends don't retry in lockstep. | Correctness |
| 2 | src/send.ts | 7–15 | Throw after the loop ends so the function can never fall through and return `undefined`. | Correctness |
| 3 | — | — | The repo has no tests even though `bun test` is configured. Add at least: retry stops after `MAX_ATTEMPTS`, 4xx (except 429) isn't retried, `sendCampaign` counts sent vs. failed correctly, and the connection is released when the query throws. Each of the bugs above would have been caught by one of these. | Test coverage |
| 4 | src/batch.ts | 4 | The new doc comment says "each send is independent", but the code also needs to say what happens on partial failure: whether it aborts, continues, or reports. | Docs |

Suggested shape for the fixes:

```ts
// send.ts
for (let attempt = 1; attempt <= MAX_ATTEMPTS; attempt++) {
  try {
    return await client.post("/messages", { to: email, template });
  } catch (err) {
    if (!isRetryable(err) || attempt === MAX_ATTEMPTS) throw err;
    await sleep(200 * 2 ** attempt + Math.random() * 100);
  }
}
throw new Error("unreachable");

// batch.ts
const conn = await pool.connect();
let recipients;
try {
  recipients = await conn.query("SELECT id, email FROM recipients WHERE campaign_id = $1", [campaignId]);
} finally {
  conn.release();
}
const CONCURRENCY = 10;
let sent = 0, failed = 0;
for (let i = 0; i < recipients.length; i += CONCURRENCY) {
  const results = await Promise.allSettled(
    recipients.slice(i, i + CONCURRENCY).map((r) => sendOne(client, r.email, template)),
  );
  for (const res of results) res.status === "fulfilled" ? sent++ : failed++;
}
return { sent, failed };
```

(If you'd rather not have the slowest send hold up each chunk, use a worker pool or `p-limit` instead of fixed chunks.)

### What Looks Good
- Pulling the retry rule out into `isRetryable` makes it clearer.
- Retrying on 429 is the right call. It just needs a retry cap and a concurrency limit to go with it.
- Releasing the connection before the long send phase, instead of holding it for the whole campaign, is a good idea. Keep it, just inside a `finally`.

### Verdict
**Request Changes.** #1 and #2 block the merge. Fix all four critical issues and add tests before merging.

